{"name":"Ceramic","hex":"#fcfff9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ceramic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of material produced by the high-temperature firing of inorganic, nonmetallic rocks and minerals."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard, brittle, inorganic, nonmetallic material, made by firing a material such as clay at a high temperature.","An object made of this material."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ceramic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ceramic","blocks":[{"text":"A ceramic is any of the various hard, brittle, heat-resistant, and corrosion-resistant materials made by shaping and then firing an inorganic, nonmetallic material, such as clay, at a high temperature. Common examples are earthenware, porcelain, and brick."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ceramic","wikidata":"Q45621"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Storage_jar_decorated_with_mountain_goats_MET_DT845.jpg/500px-Storage_jar_decorated_with_mountain_goats_MET_DT845.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Storage_jar_decorated_with_mountain_goats_MET_DT845.jpg/1280px-Storage_jar_decorated_with_mountain_goats_MET_DT845.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Storage_jar_decorated_with_mountain_goats_MET_DT845.jpg/500px-Storage_jar_decorated_with_mountain_goats_MET_DT845.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStorage_jar_decorated_with_mountain_goats_MET_DT845.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Terracotta_Panathenaic_prize_amphora_MET_DP245711.jpg/500px-Terracotta_Panathenaic_prize_amphora_MET_DP245711.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content